<header class="sg-head"><p class="featured-region">Anthem · War and march · 1570 · Europe</p><h1 class="sg-title">Wilhelmus</h1><p class="sg-local"><bdi lang="nl">Wilhelmus van Nassouwe</bdi></p><p class="sg-kid" data-say>The national anthem of the Netherlands, first sung in the 1570s in the revolt against Spain. It is the oldest national anthem still in use.</p></header>
<dl class="sg-facts"><div><dt>Words</dt><dd>anonymous (attributed to Philips of Marnix, Dirck Coornhert or Pieter Datheen)</dd></div><div><dt>Music</dt><dd>anonymous (melody of a French song of 1568)</dd></div><div><dt>Culture</dt><dd>The Dutch: the rebels of the Dutch Revolt, later the Netherlands</dd></div><div><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch</dd></div><div><dt>Place</dt><dd>Low Countries, Netherlands</dd></div><div><dt>Date</dt><dd>between 1568 and 1572; first attested 1573</dd></div><div><dt>Type</dt><dd>Anthem · War and march</dd></div><div><dt>The words</dt><dd>Public domain (lyrics anonymous (written 1568–1572; first printed 1573))</dd></div></dl>
<div class="sg-body">
<section class="sg-sec" id="story"><h2>The story</h2><p>The &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelmus">Wilhelmus</a>&quot; was written at the start of the Eighty Years' War, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>, at some time between April 1568 and the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brielle">Brielle</a> on 1 April 1572, an event it does not mention. It is first attested in 1573, sung during the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haarlem">Haarlem</a>, and in a German translation of the same year; the oldest complete <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> text is in a Geuzenliedboek (Beggars' songbook) printed in 1577–1578. Its author is not known. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philips">Philips</a> of Marnix and Dirck Coornhert were named early on, but neither ever claimed it, and its awkward rhymes make some doubt that either experienced poet wrote it; recent stylometric research has pointed to Pieter Datheen. The tune was borrowed from a Catholic French song mocking the Huguenot prince Louis of Condé's failed siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chartres">Chartres</a> in 1568, so a satire of one Protestant prince became a tribute to another.</p><p>The song is unusual among anthems in being a first-person monologue of William of Orange, the leader of the revolt. It sets out his struggle to stay loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II of Spain</a> without betraying his conscience, God and the people, placing the blame on the king's emissaries such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernando-alvarez-de-toledo-3rd-duke-of-alba">Duke of Alba</a>. The first letters of its fifteen stanzas spell &quot;Willem van Nassov&quot;, and the stanzas mirror one another around the eighth, which compares William to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> fleeing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saul">Saul</a>. In 1581 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> rejected the Spanish king's rule in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-abjuration">Act of Abjuration</a>.</p><p>For two centuries the song served as a military and political signal. Spanish musicians played it mockingly at the siege of Alkmaar in 1573; it was played at William's entry into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> in 1577 and after the liberation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/groningen">Groningen</a> in 1594. Ships of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> sounded it before engagements in colonial wars, and in the Great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambon">Ambon</a> War of 1655 a trumpeter played it to signal the assault. In the disaster year 1672 crowds sang it to press the regents to make William III stadholder. Adriaen Valerius published a slow, devotional version in 1626; in the 18th century it became a fast instrumental &quot;Princes' March&quot; of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orangists">Orangists</a>, which the ten-year-old Mozart set in seven variations at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a> in 1766. After the Batavian Revolution it was banned as a symbol of the House of Orange.</p><p>The new kingdom chose another anthem, &quot;Wien Neêrlands Bloed&quot;, adopted in 1817. But the &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelmus">Wilhelmus</a>&quot; came back, helped by the republication of Valerius's melody in 1871 and Eduard Kremser's solemn arrangement of 1877; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelmina-of-the-netherlands">Queen Wilhelmina</a> had it played at her inauguration in 1898, and on 10 May 1932 it became the official national anthem. Under the German occupation crowds sang it in demonstrations in June 1940, the authorities banned royal symbols, and the whole resistance took it up, while the collaborating NSB dropped it. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a> it was also a song of colonial rule: political prisoners who refused to sing it were sent to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boven-digoel">Boven-Digoel</a> camp, where a protest version was made to its tune, and Indonesian nationalists chose &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia-raya">Indonesia Raya</a>&quot; as their anthem as early as 1928.</p><p>Today the first stanza, sometimes followed by the sixth, is played at state ceremonies, Remembrance of the Dead, Liberation Day, King's Day, inaugurations and sporting events. Flemish nationalist rallies such as the IJzerbedevaart close with its sixth stanza.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="meaning"><h2>What it says</h2><p>William of Orange speaks in his own voice: he declares his descent, his faith in God and his loyalty to the king, and explains that conscience has forced him into revolt against the king's harsh governors. He compares himself with the biblical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a>, comforts his followers in exile and defeat, and asks God for the strength to drive out tyranny. Its tone is that of a psalm as much as a war song.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="words"><h2>The words</h2><div class="sg-show" role="group" aria-label="Show these columns"><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-col="orig">Dutch</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-col="en">In English</button></div><div class="sg-blocks"><div class="sg-lyrics sg-cols-2"><div class="sg-colhead" aria-hidden="true"><span class="sg-o">Dutch</span><span class="sg-e">In English</span></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Wilhelmus van Nassouwe</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>William of Nassau</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">ben ik, van Duitsen bloed,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>am I, of Dutch blood;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">den vaderland getrouwe</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>faithful to the fatherland</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">blijf ik tot in den dood.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>I remain until death.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Een Prinse van Oranje</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>A Prince of Orange</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">ben ik, vrij, onverveerd,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>am I, free, unafraid;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">den Koning van Hispanje</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>the King of Spain</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">heb ik altijd geëerd.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>I have always honoured.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">In Godes vrees te leven</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>To live in the fear of God</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">heb ik altijd betracht,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>I have always striven;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">daarom ben ik verdreven,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>therefore I am driven out,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">om land, om luid gebracht.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>bereft of land, of people.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Maar God zal mij regeren</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>But God will govern me</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">als een goed instrument,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>as a good instrument,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">dat ik zal wederkeren</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>so that I shall return</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">in mijnen regiment.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>into my rule.</span></p></div><details class="sg-more"><summary>Show all 120 lines</summary><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Lijdt u, mijn onderzaten</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Bear it patiently, my subjects,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">die oprecht zijt van aard,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>who are upright by nature;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">God zal u niet verlaten,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>God will not forsake you,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">al zijt gij nu bezwaard.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>though you are now burdened.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Die vroom begeert te leven,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Whoever wishes to live piously,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">bidt God nacht ende dag,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>let him pray to God night and day</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">dat Hij mij kracht zal geven,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>that He will give me strength,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">dat ik u helpen mag.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>that I may help you.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Lijf en goed al te samen</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Life and goods all together</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">heb ik u niet verschoond,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>I have not spared for you;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">mijn broeders hoog van namen</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>my brothers, high of name,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">hebben 't u ook vertoond:</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>have also shown it to you:</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Graaf Adolf is gebleven</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Count Adolf has fallen</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">in Friesland in den slag,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>in Friesland, in the battle;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">zijn ziel in 't eeuwig leven</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>his soul in eternal life</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">verwacht den jongsten dag.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>awaits the Last Day.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Edel en hooggeboren,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Noble and high-born,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">van keizerlijken stam,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>of imperial stock,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">een vorst des rijks verkoren,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>chosen a prince of the Empire,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">als een vroom christenman,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>as a pious Christian man,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">voor Godes woord geprezen,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>praised for God's word,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">heb ik, vrij onversaagd,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>I have, free and undaunted,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">als een held zonder vrezen</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>as a hero without fear</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">mijn edel bloed gewaagd.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>ventured my noble blood.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Mijn schild ende betrouwen</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>My shield and my trust</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">zijt Gij, o God mijn Heer,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>are You, O God my Lord;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">op U zo wil ik bouwen,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>on You I will build,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Verlaat mij nimmermeer.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>forsake me nevermore.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Dat ik doch vroom mag blijven,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>That I may yet remain pious,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">uw dienaar t'aller stond,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>your servant at every hour,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">de tirannie verdrijven</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>and drive out the tyranny</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">die mij mijn hart doorwondt.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>that wounds me through my heart.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Van al die mij bezwaren</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>From all who burden me</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">en mijn vervolgers zijn,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>and are my persecutors,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">mijn God, wil doch bewaren</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>my God, be pleased to keep</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">den trouwen dienaar dijn,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>your faithful servant,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">dat zij mij niet verrassen</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>that they do not take me by surprise</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">in hunnen bozen moed,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>in their wicked intent,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">hun handen niet en wassen</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>do not wash their hands</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">in mijn onschuldig bloed.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>in my innocent blood.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Als David moeste vluchten</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>As David had to flee</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">voor Sauel den tiran,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>before Saul the tyrant,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">zo heb ik moeten zuchten</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>so I have had to sigh</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">als menig edelman.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>as many a nobleman.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Maar God heeft hem verheven,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>But God has raised him up,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">verlost uit alder nood,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>delivered him from all distress,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">een koninkrijk gegeven</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>given him a kingdom</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">in Israël zeer groot.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>in Israel, very great.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Na 't zuur zal ik ontvangen</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>After the sour I shall receive</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">van God mijn Heer dat zoet,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>from God my Lord the sweet;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">daarna zo doet verlangen</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>for that so longs</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">mijn vorstelijk gemoed:</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>my princely heart:</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">dat is, dat ik mag sterven</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>that is, that I may die</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">met eren in dat veld,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>with honour on the field,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">een eeuwig rijk verwerven</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>and win an eternal kingdom</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">als een getrouwen held.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>as a faithful hero.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Niet doet mij meer erbarmen</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Nothing moves me more to pity</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">in mijnen wederspoed</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>in my adversity</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">dan dat men ziet verarmen</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>than that one sees impoverished</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">des Konings landen goed.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>the King's good lands.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Dat u de Spanjaards krenken,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>That the Spaniards wrong you,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">o edel Neerland zoet,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>O noble, sweet Netherland,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">als ik daaraan gedenke,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>when I think of it,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">mijn edel hart dat bloedt.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>my noble heart, it bleeds.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Als een prins opgezeten</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>As a prince on horseback</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">met mijner heires-kracht,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>with the strength of my army,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">van den tiran vermeten</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>from the arrogant tyrant</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">heb ik den slag verwacht,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>I awaited the battle;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">die, bij Maastricht begraven,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>he, dug in by Maastricht,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">bevreesde mijn geweld;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>feared my force;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">mijn ruiters zag men draven</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>my horsemen were seen riding</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">zeer moedig door dat veld.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>most boldly through the field.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Zo het den wil des Heren</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>If it had been the will of the Lord</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">op dien tijd had geweest,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>at that time,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">had ik geern willen keren</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>I would gladly have turned away</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">van u dit zwaar tempeest.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>from you this heavy tempest.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Maar de Heer van hierboven,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>But the Lord from up above,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">die alle ding regeert,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>who rules all things,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">die men altijd moet loven,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>whom one must always praise,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">en heeft het niet begeerd.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>did not desire it.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Zeer christlijk was gedreven</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Very Christian was the drive</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">mijn prinselijk gemoed,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>of my princely heart;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">standvastig is gebleven</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>steadfast has remained</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">mijn hart in tegenspoed.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>my heart in adversity.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Den Heer heb ik gebeden</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>The Lord I have prayed</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">uit mijnes harten grond,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>from the bottom of my heart</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">dat Hij mijn zaak wil redden,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>that He will save my cause,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">mijn onschuld maken kond.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>make my innocence known.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Oorlof, mijn arme schapen</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Farewell, my poor sheep,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">die zijt in groten nood,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>who are in great distress;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">uw herder zal niet slapen,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>your shepherd will not sleep,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">al zijt gij nu verstrooid.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>though you are now scattered.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Tot God wilt u begeven,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Turn to God,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">zijn heilzaam woord neemt aan,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>take up his saving word,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">als vrome christen leven,-</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>live as pious Christians,-</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">'t zal hier haast zijn gedaan.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>it will soon be over here.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">Voor God wil ik belijden</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Before God I will confess,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">en zijner groten macht,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>and before his great might,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">dat ik tot genen tijden</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>that at no time</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">den Koning heb veracht,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>have I despised the King,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">dan dat ik God den Heere,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>except that God the Lord,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">der hoogsten Majesteit,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>the highest Majesty,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">heb moeten obediëren</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>I have had to obey</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="nl">in der gerechtigheid.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>in righteousness.</span></p></div></details></div></div><div class="sg-credit"><p>Original: Anonymous (c. 1570); the original text. Text from <a href="https://nl.wikisource.org/wiki/Het_Wilhelmus" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikisource</a>; public domain.</p><p>The English is the Institute&#8217;s own translation, made from the original for this page.</p></div><details class="sg-notes"><summary>Notes on the translation (19)</summary><ul><li>The first letters of the fifteen stanzas spell WILLEM VAN NASSOV (William of Nassau); the acrostic is lost in translation and could be mentioned on the page.</li><li>The source text is in modernized spelling (as on Wikisource), not the 1570s orthography; it was translated as given.</li><li>line 1.2: 'Duitsen' (Duytschen) in the 16th century meant 'Dutch' in the old wide sense, of the Low German and Dutch lands, not 'German' in today's sense; William's family was from Nassau in Germany. Both senses are argued; editor should choose how to gloss it.</li><li>line 1.7-1.8 and stanza 15: the song presents William as loyal to Philip II and fighting only his ministers (Alba), the official line of the revolt at the time.</li><li>line 2.4: 'om land, om luid gebracht' = deprived of land and people ('luid' = people, subjects).</li><li>line 2.8: 'regiment' = rule, government (his offices as stadholder), not a military regiment.</li><li>line 3.1: 'Lijdt u' = be patient, endure (it).</li><li>line 4.2: 'heb ik u niet verschoond' = I have not spared (withheld) for your sake; it does not mean he did not spare the subjects.</li><li>line 4.5: 'is gebleven' = remained (on the field), i.e. fell: Adolf of Nassau, killed at Heiligerlee in 1568.</li><li>line 5.3: 'een vorst des rijks verkoren' is unclear: 'chosen' may mean elevated or simply 'a chosen prince of the (Holy Roman) Empire'.</li><li>line 6.8: 'die mij mijn hart doorwondt' = that wounds my heart through (pierces me to the heart).</li><li>line 9.3-9.4: 'daarna zo doet verlangen mijn vorstelijk gemoed' = for that my princely heart (mind) longs; word order kept.</li><li>line 10.4: 'des Konings landen goed' can be read as 'the King's good lands' or 'the King's lands and their goods'.</li><li>line 11.3: 'vermeten' = presumptuous, arrogant; the tyrant is the Duke of Alba.</li><li>line 11.5: 'bij Maastricht begraven' = entrenched (dug in) near Maastricht, in 1568; not 'buried'.</li><li>line 11.7: 'draven' is literally 'trot'; rendered 'riding'.</li><li>line 13.1: 'Zeer christlijk was gedreven mijn prinselijk gemoed' = my princely mind (heart) was driven in a very Christian way; rendered loosely in word order.</li><li>line 14.1: 'Oorlof' = farewell (literally leave, permission to go).</li><li>line 8.2: 'Sauel' is the old form of Saul, kept as the name.</li></ul></details></section>
